===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sed-|*-dʰlom}}
From {{inh|en|enm|sadel|t=seat placed on the back of a horse, etc., for riding}}{{nb...|(Late Middle English) saddle, saddull, (Middle English) saddell, saddil, saddill, saddyll, sadell, sadelle, sadil, sadill, sadille, saddul, sadle, sadul, sadulle, sadyl, sadyle, sadyll, sadylle, satel|otherforms=1}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=sā̆del|pos=n|id=MED38238}}</ref> from {{inh|en|ang|sadel}}, {{m|ang|sadol|t=saddle}}{{nb...|(Late Old English) sædel, (Old English) sadal (Northumbria), sadul|otherforms=1}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*sadulaz|t=saddle}}; further etymology uncertain, perhaps from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*sod-dʰlo-}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*sed-|t=to sit}} + {{m|ine-pro|*-dʰlom}} (a variant of {{m|ine-pro|*-trom|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming {{glossary|noun}}s denoting instruments or tools}}), though the ''{{w|Oxford English Dictionary}}'' says this “presents formal difficulties”.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''n.''{{sup|1}} and ''adj.''|noformat=1|id=169618|date=June 2022|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref>

