====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|tack}} A [[seat#Noun|seat]] for a [[rider]], often [[make#Verb|made]] of [[leather#Noun|leather]] and [[raise#Verb|raised]] in the [[front#Noun|front]] and [[rear#Noun|rear]], [[place#Verb|placed]] on the [[back#Noun|back]] of a [[horse#Noun|horse]] or other [[animal]], and [[secure#Verb|secured]] by a [[strap#Noun|strap]] around the animal's [[body#Noun|body]].
## A [[similar#Adjective|similar]] [[implement#Noun|implement]] [[use#Verb|used]] to secure [[good#Noun|goods]] to animals; a [[packsaddle]].
## {{synonym of|en|harness saddle|t=the [[part#Noun|part]] of a [[harness#Noun|harness]] which [[support#Verb|supports]] the [[weight#Noun|weight]] of [[pole#Noun|poles]] or [[shaft#Noun|shafts]] [[attach]]ing a [[vehicle]] to a horse or other animal}}
## A [[cushion#Noun|cushion]] used as a seat in a [[cart#Noun|cart]] or other vehicle.
## The [[immovable#Adjective|immovable]] seat of a [[bicycle#Noun|bicycle]], [[motorcycle#Noun|motorcycle]], or similar vehicle.
## {{lb|en|by extension}}
### ''Chiefly followed by'' '''[[the#Article|the]]''': [[horseriding|horse-riding]] as an [[activity]] or [[occupation]].
### {{synonym of|en|saddle brown|t=a [[medium#Adjective|medium]] [[brown#Adjective|brown]] [[colour#Noun|colour]], like that of saddle leather}}
###: {{color panel|634739}}
# Something [[resemble|resembling]] a saddle ''(sense 1)'' in [[appearance]] or [[shape#Noun|shape]].
## A [[low#Adjective|low]] [[point#Noun|point]], in the shape of a saddle, between [[two]] [[hill#Noun|hills]].
##* '''1926''', {{w|T. E. Lawrence}}, ''Seven Pillars of Wisdom'', New York: Anchor (1991), p. 180:
##*: After fifteen minutes of this we were glad to reach a high '''saddle''' on which former travellers had piled little cairns of commemoration and thankfulness.
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=1960|month=December|author=Voyageur|title=The Mountain Railways of the Bernese Oberland|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=752|text=So we continue climbing to the '''saddle''' of the Kleine Scheidegg, where ahead there comes into view the wide expanse of the Grindelwald valley, backed by the snowy crown of the Wetterhorn.}}
##* '''1977''', {{w|John Le Carré}}, ''The Honourable Schoolboy'', Folio Society 2010, p. 483:
##*: With Lizzie leading, they scrambled quickly over several false peaks towards the '''saddle'''.
## A [[cut#Noun|cut]] of [[meat#Noun|meat]] that [[include]]s both [[loin]]s and part of the [[backbone]].
##* '''1870''', ''The Cook and Housewife's Manual'' (5th edition)
##*: A modern refinement is to put laver in the dripping-pan, which, in basting, imparts a high gout: or a large '''saddle''' may be served over a pound and a half of laver, stewed in brown sauce with catsup {{...}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1958|year_published=1972|author=Anthony Burgess|authorlink=Anthony Burgess|title=The Enemy in the Blanket|series=The Malayan Trilogy|page=272|passage=Certainly, in the gravy soups, turbot, hare, roast '''saddles''', cabinet puddings, boiled eggs at tea-time and bread and butter and meat paste with the morning tray, one tasted one's own decadence[.]}}
## {{lb|en|construction}}
### A [[small#Adjective|small]] [[sloped#Adjective|sloped]] or [[tapered#Adjective|tapered]] [[structure#Noun|structure]] that [[help#Verb|helps]] [[channel#Verb|channel]] [[surface water]] to [[drain#Noun|drains]].
### The [[raised#Adjective|raised]] [[floorboard]] in a [[doorway]].
## {{lb|en|dentistry}} The part of a [[denture]] which [[hold#Verb|holds]] the [[artificial]] [[tooth#Noun|teeth]].
## {{lb|en|engineering}} An [[equipment]] part, such as a [[flange#Noun|flange]], which is [[hollow out|hollowed out]] to [[fit#Verb|fit]] upon a [[convex#Adjective|convex]] [[surface#Noun|surface]] and [[serve#Verb|serve]] as a [[means#Noun|means]] of [[attachment]] or [[support#Noun|support]].
## {{lb|en|geology}} An {{l|en|anticline|t=[[fold#Noun|fold]] with [[stratum|strata]] [[slop#Verb|sloping]] [[downwards]] on each [[side#Noun|side]]}}; specifically, a [[depression]] [[locate]]d along the [[axial#Adjective|axial]] [[trend#Noun|trend]] of such a fold.
### {{lb|en|chiefly|Australia|mining}} {{synonym of|en|saddle reef|t=a saddle-[[shaped#Adjective|shaped]] [[bed#Verb|bedded]] [[mineral#Noun|mineral]] (usually [[gold-bearing]] [[quartz]]) [[vein#Noun|vein]] [[occur]]ring along the [[crest#Noun|crest]] of an anticline or {{lb|en|less common}} a [[syncline]] (an [[inverted#Adjective|inverted]] saddle)}}
## {{lb|en|geometry}} {{synonym of|en|saddle point|t=a point in the [[range#Noun|range]] of a [[smooth#Adjective|smooth]] [[function#Noun|function]], every [[neighbourhood]] of which [[contain]]s points on each side of its [[tangent#Adjective|tangent]] [[plane#Noun|plane]]}}
## {{lb|en|lutherie}}
### The part of a [[guitar#Noun|guitar]] which supports the [[string#Noun|strings]] and, in an [[acoustic guitar]], [[transfer#Verb|transfers]] their [[vibration]]s through the [[bridge#Noun|bridge]] to the [[soundboard]].
### A small [[object#Noun|object]] ([[traditionally]] made of [[ebony]]) at the bottom of a [[string instrument]] such as a [[cello]], [[viola]], or [[violin]] below the [[tailpiece]] on which the {{l|en|tailgut|t=[[cord#Noun|cord]] securing the tailpiece to the [[instrument]]}} [[rest#Verb|rests]].
## {{lb|en|nautical}} A [[block#Noun|block]] of [[wood#Noun|wood]] with [[concave#Adjective|concave]] depressions at the [[top#Noun|top]] and [[bottom#Noun|bottom]], usually [[fasten]]ed to one [[spar#Noun|spar]] and [[shape#Verb|shaped]] to [[receive#Verb|receive]] the [[end#Noun|end]] of another.
## {{lb|en|zoology}}
### The [[clitellum]] of an [[earthworm]] ([[family]] [[Lumbricidae]]).
### The [[lower#Adjective|lower]] part of the back of a [[domestic]] [[fowl#Noun|fowl]], especially a [[male#Adjective|male]] [[bird#Noun|bird]], bearing the [[saddle feather]]s or [[saddle hackle]]s.
### ''In full'' '''saddle marking''' ''or'' '''saddle patch''': a [[saddlelike|saddle-like]] [[marking#Noun|marking]] on an animal, such as one on the back of an [[adult#Adjective|adult]] [[harp seal]] or [[saddleback seal]] ({{taxlink|Pagophilus groenlandicus|species|ver=20221008}}), or any of [[numerous]] such markings on a [[boa constrictor]] (''[[Boa constrictor]]'').
## {{lb|en|originally|and|chiefly|Canada|US}}
### A piece of leather [[stitch#Verb|stitched]] across the [[instep]] of a [[shoe#Noun|shoe]], usually having a [[different#Adjective|different]] [[colour#Noun|colour]] from the [[rest#Noun|rest]] of the shoe.
### {{synonym of|en|saddle oxford}} ''or'' '''[[saddle shoe]]''' (“a shoe, [[resemble|resembling]] an [[oxford]], which has a saddle ''(sense 11.1)''”)
###* '''1972''', Judy Blume, ''Tales of a Fourth Grade Nothing'' (page 56)
###*: 'Brown-and-white '''saddles''' for Fudge and loafers for Peter.' / 'OK, Peter... let's see how those feet have grown.' / I slipped out of my old shoes and stood up.

